# Launcher scripts are read by the shell of the machine they run on, and each
# one is strict about line endings in a different direction. Pinned here so a
# checkout on another platform cannot silently normalise them: cmd.exe tracks
# byte offsets when it follows `goto`, and bash treats a trailing CR as part of
# the command and fails on it.
#
# Deliberately scoped to these extensions rather than a repo-wide `text=auto`,
# which would renormalise every file in the project on the next checkout.
*.bat       text eol=crlf
*.cmd       text eol=crlf
*.command   text eol=lf
*.sh        text eol=lf
